-- title:
--   Surjectivity of the trace of a prime-order ring automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a finite reduced commutative ring, let $\tau : R \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } R$ be a ring automorphism of $R$, and let $\ell$ be a prime number such that $\tau^{\ell}$ is the identity automorphism. Assume the following residual non-triviality hypothesis: for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $R$ with $\tau(\mathfrak{m}) \subseteq \mathfrak{m}$ there exists an element $x \in R$ with $\tau(x) - x \notin \mathfrak{m}$, i.e. the automorphism induced by $\tau$ on the residue field $R/\mathfrak{m}$ is not the identity. Then for every $c \in R$ fixed by $\tau$, that is with $\tau(c) = c$, there exists $u \in R$ whose trace along the cyclic group generated by $\tau$ equals $c$: $$\sum_{i=0}^{\ell-1} \tau^{i}(u) = c.$$ Thus, under these hypotheses, the trace map $u \mapsto \sum_{i<\ell} \tau^{i}(u)$ from $R$ to the subring of $\tau$-fixed elements is surjective. No separate hypothesis that $\tau$ has exact order $\ell$ is imposed, only $\tau^{\ell} = 1$.
--
--   This is the additive counterpart of the surjectivity of the norm for an automorphism of prime order acting non-trivially on each stable residue field, in the style of the classical computation of traces in cyclic extensions of finite fields. It supplies a residual surjectivity input to [`AutomorphicForm.exists_normString_eq_toTensorGL_of_mem_localIntegralSet_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one_of_prime`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_normString_eq_toTensorGL_of_mem_localIntegralSet_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one_of_prime), where it is applied to residue algebras of a commutative order in order to start a successive-approximation argument at a place unramified in a cyclic extension of prime degree.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Finite_exists_sum_pow_apply_eq_of_isReduced_of_prime.lean

